{"base_rate":0.19701492537313434,"brier":0.11389970149253732,"bss":0.2800273741128758,"bss_hi":0.403420167132359,"bss_lo":0.12325739431934077,"chart":{"base":[232.3,168.9],"fp":[222.4,141.1],"lead":"62,257 272,239.6 482,230.4 692,217","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 49% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 58% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 2%; promised 91% → rained 67%"},"rel":"72.3,457.4 350.4,358.8 636.8,176.9"},"country":"BF","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09316417910447758,"ess":344.79230769230793,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ouagadougou</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ouagadougou rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 670 days, 2024-04-27 to\n2026-03-24. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 111 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(52&ndash;172) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>334</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ouagadougou</b> <span class=\"muted\">Burkina Faso</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;20% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 20% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>52&ndash;172\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>670 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ouagadougou &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ouagadougou\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.52994011976048,379.8203592814371 89.96567164179103,322.23880597014926 169.17812500000002,222.75 267.2191304347825,123.50724637681157 352.4967647058823,50.117647058823536 409.50117647058823,18.0 409.50117647058823,28.70588235294116 352.4967647058823,114.35294117647055 267.2191304347825,207.91304347826087 169.17812500000002,308.0625 89.96567164179103,371.13432835820896 58.52994011976048,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"310.28656716417913\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"310.28656716417913\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.52994011976048,380.9101796407186 89.96567164179103,343.97014925373134 169.17812500000002,319.4375 267.2191304347825,265.94202898550725 352.4967647058823,167.88235294117646 409.50117647058823,109.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 334 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.52994011976048\" cy=\"380.9101796407186\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"89.96567164179103\" cy=\"343.97014925373134\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"169.17812500000002\" cy=\"319.4375\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 59%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"267.2191304347825\" cy=\"265.94202898550725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"352.4967647058823\" cy=\"167.88235294117646\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.50117647058823\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(20%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ouagadougou the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.34) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.01).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.009</td><td class='num'>23.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>149</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.086</td><td class='num'>7.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.340</td><td class='num'>8.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":12.36566,"lon":-1.53388,"n":670,"n_cities":216,"name":"Ouagadougou","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0014970059880239522,"n":334,"obs":0.0029940119760479044,"sig":false},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09029850746268656,"n":67,"obs":0.1044776119402985,"sig":false},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.3140625,"n":64,"obs":0.171875,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.591014492753623,"n":69,"obs":0.3188405797101449,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.8319117647058822,"n":68,"obs":0.5882352941176471,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9929411764705882,"n":68,"obs":0.75,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.7,"provisional":false,"rank":111,"rank_hi":172.0,"rank_lo":51.975,"reliability":0.021597997525590197,"resolution":0.06778044278303504,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"ouagadougou","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Ouagadougou"}